-- title:
--   Level-M' reduction through the Igusa branch lies over s
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$; its residue field is written $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   Three function fields occur. First, $\overline{\mathcal F}(M') =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, itself generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}_d(j_q)$ for the divisors $d$ of $M'$. Second, $\overline{\mathcal F}_q(M') =$ `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of `xHFunctionField (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Third, over any field $K$, `modularFunctionFieldC K M'` is the intermediate field of $K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(K)$ generated by $j_q$ and by $\mathrm{qExpand}_{M'}(j_q)$ with coefficients in $K$. A place of $F$ over $K$ ([`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22)) is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $K$, different from $F$, whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring; it is rational when $K$ maps onto its residue field, `evalAt` is the resulting $K$-valued evaluation, and `ord` is the normalised order.
--
--   The data fixed at the outset are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` over $\kappa_A$ with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ_A`, that is, of the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ_A M' w`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa_A\,M') \in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa_A$; a chosen element $s$ of $W$; the inclusion `hle` of $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ in $\overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$; and a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ to `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'`, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, the conditions that a constant lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it lies in $A$ and reduces to its image in $\kappa_A$, that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, that $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserves degrees, and the pushforward compatibility of divisors with residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that $R_0$ is the coefficientwise (Gauss) reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ lies in $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. The hypothesis `hGU` is a uniqueness statement for $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$: any valuation subring $V$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ that traces $A$ on the constants, contains the element $j_q$ (the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $j$, which lies in $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$), and has the property that for every polynomial $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with all coefficients in $A$ the membership of $p(j_q)$ in the maximal ideal of $V$ forces every coefficient of $p$ to lie in the maximal ideal of $V$, satisfies $V = R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ as sets.
--
--   The base data on the constant side are: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), and, writing $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation ring of $k_0$, the hypotheses that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), that its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$. The field $\overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   Under these standing hypotheses the assertion is a nested universal statement. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$ such that the join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $F_0$ is all of $\overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$, and such that $F_0$ is linearly disjoint from the constants in the following sense: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is finite-dimensional over $k_0$, every $m$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$, and every family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$ with all $a_i$ in the join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ satisfying the three clauses: an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal.
--
--   Let $O$ be a subring of $F_0$ which is local and Noetherian, such that $O \subseteq W_0$; an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in $O$; every $f \in O$ is congruent, in the sense that the difference is not a unit of $O$, to the image of some $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ and image in $O$; and $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $O$, in the sense that every $f \in F_0$ can be written as $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in O$ and $h \ne 0$.
--
--   Let $E_0$ be a natural number with $1 \le E_0$, let the image of $\pi_0$ lie in $O$ (`hπO`), let $c_x, c_y \in O$, let $u$ be a unit of $O$, let $\widehat{A_0}$ denote the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat{A_0}\,(\pi_0^{E_0})$, that is, $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,\widehat{A_0}$ modulo the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi_0^{E_0}$, and let $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ be units of this crossing model. The crossing-presentation hypotheses are: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of each $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ and image in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$ in $\widehat{A_0}$; $\iota$ carries the image of $c_x$ to $\gamma_U \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U` and the image of $c_y$ to $\gamma_V \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V`; the element $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and, whenever it lies in $W_0$, in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; and $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, does not lie in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   Let $W_x$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ subject to the following clauses: $O \subseteq W_x$; an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in $W_x$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_x$ and generates its maximal ideal; there is an element $t \in W_x$ with the Gauss property that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, the membership of $p(t)$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ forces every coefficient of $p$ to lie in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal; $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; and $c_y$, whenever it lies in $W_x$, does not. Finally, $W_x$ is required to satisfy an integrality clause relating it to $R_0$: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and which has nonnegative order at every place $P$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j_q$ has nonnegative order, the image of $g$ under the inclusion `hle` lies in $F_0$, that element lies in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g) = 0$, and if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then that element lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and image in $O$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g))$, the difference of the element and the image of $c$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   Let $F_I$ be a field with a $\kappa_A$-algebra structure and let $R_x$ be a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$ to $F_I$, i.e. a valuation subring $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}_q(M')$ with a surjective ring homomorphism $R_x.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $F_I$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, tracing $A$ on the constants and reducing them through $\kappa_A$, and with the property that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant. It is assumed that $R_x$ traces $W_x$ on $F_0$, i.e. for $f \in F_0$ the image of $f$ lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when $f \in W_x$, and that $R_x$ traces $R_0$ on the level-$M'$ field, i.e. for $f \in \overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ the image of $f$ under `hle` lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$. Let $b_x$ be a rational place of $F_I$ over $\kappa_A$ such that $R_x.\mathrm{residue}$ sends every element of $O$ that lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ into the valuation subring of $b_x$, and sends every such element which is not a unit of $O$ into the maximal ideal of that valuation subring.
--
--   The conclusion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $j :$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` $\to F_I$ with the following two properties. First, for every $f \in \overline{\mathcal F}(M')$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, the image of $f$ under the inclusion `hle` lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$ and $R_x.\mathrm{residue}$ of that image equals $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$. Second, for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'`, the element $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$.
--
--   This is the step on the Igusa component which shows that the reduction attached to the branch $W_x$ computes the level-$M'$ reduction through a single ring homomorphism of the level-$M'$ function field over $\kappa_A$ into the reduced field $F_I$, and that under this homomorphism the branch place $b_x$ lies exactly over the chosen supersingular place $s$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_branchPlace_igusaEnd_integral_overS_of_node_crossingPresentation_igusaBranch) in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
